      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "consequence",
      "statement": "The harness has a setjmp recovery path that cleans up and returns before the row loop if the duplicate-call report raises a libpng error. The supplied numbered evidence does not establish whether png_app_error warns or raises that error under this setup.",
      "evidence": [
        {"unit_id": "u-e9cdca141412a92154b2", "start_line": 146, "end_line": 150, "role": "primary", "dependency_reason": ""},
        {"unit_id": "u-e9cdca141412a92154b2", "start_line": 169, "end_line": 175, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "Places the duplicate-call candidate before row reading."},
        {"unit_id": "u-02b6226984a9ddec355c", "start_line": 304, "end_line": 310, "role": "dependency", "dependency_reason": "Identifies png_app_error as the report path whose behavior is decisive."}
      ],
      "absence_claim": false,
      "audited_unit_ids": []
    },
    {
      "topic": "alternative",
      "statement": "When row state is not initialized, png_start_read_image itself initializes it. A supplied library test also shows a read_info → start_read_image → read_row sequence; that test does not establish an alternative call sequence for the fixed harness.",
